WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.500
Namaste, and welcome to EduLe. I am Meera Iyer,

00:01.500 --> 00:04.000
and in the next twenty minutes you will write
your first real Python program — no experience needed.

00:04.000 --> 00:08.000
First, we open the editor and print our first line.
Python reads almost like English: print, brackets,
and your words in quotes.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.000
Next, variables. Think of a variable as a labelled
box: we store a name, a number, or a list of expenses,
and Python remembers it for us.

00:13.000 --> 00:17.000
Now the useful part: we take a messy list of monthly
expenses and ask Python to add them up, find the
biggest one, and show the total in rupees.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.000
We add one condition — if the total crosses your
budget, Python warns you. That is the whole idea
of programming: rules that do the boring work for you.

00:19.000 --> 00:20.000
Finally, we save the script and run it again
with different numbers. Change the data, keep the program.
